A||||5||Racer 1||T-Tops need help!  8-)
Z||000000||Racer 1||06-04-99||11:13 PM||||Hey I have T-tops on my fiero and was wondering were I can get new rubber seals and some parts for them! I tried looking in the haynes and chilton manuals but they dont even mention t-tops!I you can give me some help I would appreciate it!!!!
Z||000001||FieroMike||06-05-99||11:08 AM||||Racer 1,<br>They do not make t-top Fieros.  That is an aftermarket option. (90% sure of that)  I would try bringing a piece of it in to a local parts store and just try and match it up to something.  You might try asking the guys at PISA corp also.
Z||000002||mrfiero||06-05-99||11:05 PM||||Fieros indeed came with T-Tops.  They were designed and installed by C&C of Brighton, MI.  They were originally sold as kits and installed by authorized dealers, but in 1988 they were an "official" option complete with their own RPO code (CJB).  I currently own an '88 Formula with T-Tops.....#1186 out of 1245 factory installed in '88.  Some parts are still available, but many have been discontinued.  What exactly do you need?    
Z||000003||Racer 1||06-06-99||02:52 PM||||I need the grey plastic piece that goes on the front part plastic piece.its the piece were the metal t-top rod slide into to lock it into the cars chassis.And I need new rubber pieces that hold the inside trim up.This piece is right next to the t-tops main rubber seal!And also my t-top inside metal pieces rattle and might need new bushings if there is any in there? Thanks for ya help!
Z||000004||Bozone||06-08-99||04:55 PM||||Speaking of T-Tops, I have heard of one in the area that is for sale. Haven't seen it but a friend did. He said it was a little beat. Never heard of a T-Top Fiero so he thought it was a hack job. When I told him there WAS such a thing, he got interested again. The seller wanted $1100 but that might be negotiable. If the car is beat a bit though, what might it be worth? If there was only 1200+ made, maybe it's worth the trouble to get it.
Z||000005||mrfiero||06-14-99||05:22 AM||||Let me re-phrase something....there were 1245 '88 Fieros with T-Tops.  '88 was the only year it was sanctioned by GM and received an official RPO code.  There a few thousand retrofit kits built (identical to the '88 version, except for the weatherseals).  If your car or the car you're thinking about buying is  an '84-'87 then it was an aftermarket kit....all T-Tops for the Fiero were built by the same company (C&C Skylite) and were installed by trained installers at various sunroof shops  around the country.  That said, $1100 isn't a bad price for a Fiero with T-Tops and it becomes a better deal if it's an '88.  The drawback is parts are becoming scarce.....so if it needs new weatherseals, or whatever then it becomes expensive locating this stuff.  I know the P-seals are discontinued as well as one of the main weatherseals.  I hope this clears it up a little.       
